ESTABLISHING VEHICLE PARAMETERS

2-DOF Quarter-Car Suspension Model
Vehicle: Tata Harrier

This file establishes the vehicle and suspension parameters required for the development of the 2-DOF quarter-car model.

The parameters are divided into:

1. Vehicle mass parameters
2. Suspension parameters
3. Tire parameter

The initial values represent the baseline suspension configuration. These values are later used as the reference for suspension parameter optimization.

VEHICLE PARAMETERS

Unsprung mass

Represents the wheel, tire, and other components associated with the wheel assembly.

m1 = 40 kg

Sprung mass

Represents the portion of the vehicle body supported by the suspension in the quarter-car model.

m2 = 400 kg

BASELINE SUSPENSION PARAMETERS

Suspension stiffness

ks = 20000 N/m

Suspension damping

cs = 1500 Ns/m

TIRE PARAMETER

Tire stiffness

kt = 190000 N/m

PARAMETER SUMMARY

Parameter          Symbol       Value       Unit

Unsprung mass      m1           40          kg
Sprung mass        m2           400         kg
Suspension         ks           20000       N/m
stiffness

Suspension         cs           1500        Ns/m
damping

